//! # Boss actors (`d_en_bossNP`, REL module 4)
//!
//! **Synthetic-base warning.** Every `0x80C...` address below is an analysis
//! address from the REL-to-ELF conversion: the module is placed at the
//! synthetic slot `0x80C00000` and the entry point is `0x80C000F0`. These are
//! **not runtime addresses**. The loader chooses the real REL base at boot, so
//! do not compare these values with a live game or with memory dumps. Calls
//! into `main.dol` (for example `0x8015F7C0`) are absolute DOL addresses and
//! are unaffected by the REL base.
//!
//! ## What this module covers
//!
//! This module is the reconstruction of `d_en_bossNP`, the boss-actor REL. The
//! first pass translated 23 functions, the wave-3 second pass added 20, the
//! wave-4 pass added 24, the wave-5 pass added 25, the wave-6 pass added 25,
//! the wave-10 pass added 25, the wave-12 pass added 24, the wave-13 pass
//! added 25, the wave-14 pass added 25, the wave-15 pass added 25, the
//! wave-16 pass added 25, the wave-17 pass added 25, the wave-19 pass added
//! 25, the wave-20 pass added 25, the wave-21 pass added 25, the wave-22 pass
//! added 25, the wave-23 pass added 25, the wave-24 pass added 25, the wave-25
//! pass added 25, the wave-26 pass added 24 state-id factories, the wave-27
//! pass added 24 bodies (twenty state-id factories and four destructor
//! adapters), the wave-28 pass added 20 bodies (fourteen Morton state-id
//! factories and six destructor adapters), the wave-29 pass added 24
//! bodies (seventeen Roy and five Wendy state-id factories and the Larry
//! destructor pair), the wave-30 pass added 24 bodies (the twelve remaining
//! Wendy state-id factories and six destructor-adapter pairs), the wave-31
//! pass added 23 bodies (thirteen state-id factories and the five remaining
//! destructor-adapter pairs), the wave-32 pass added 22 state-id factories
//! (two whole runs: thirteen at `0x80C3D1F0` and nine at `0x80C37D60`), and
//! the wave-33 pass adds 45 state-id factories (all of the `0x80C20000`
//! bucket's factory runs: sixteen at `0x80C211E0`, sixteen at `0x80C218D0`,
//! one at `0x80C292D0`, four at `0x80C2A4A0`, six at `0x80C2C430` and two at
//! `0x80C2FDB0`), and the wave-34 pass adds 84 bodies (eighty-three 12-byte
//! constant/address factories across the remaining `0x80C0`, `0x80C1`,
//! `0x80C3` and `0x80C4` buckets, plus the `0x80C38230` virtual-dispatch
//! wrapper), for 756 in total; the wave-107 pass adds the eight bodies whose
//! C export truncated at `halt_baddata()`, recovered from the raw REL text, for
//! 764 in total; the wave-113 pass adds the last two truncated-export
//! bodies in the `0x80C40000` bucket, also recovered from the raw REL text, for
//! 766 in total; and the wave-114 pass adds the last two truncated-export
//! bodies in the `0x80C50000` bucket, for 768 in total; the wave-117 pass
//! adds the last truncated-export body in the `0x80C00000` bucket, for 769 in
//! total; and the wave-118 pass adds the last truncated-export body in the
//! `0x80C20000` bucket, for 770 in total. Wave 246 converts the first
//! twenty-five of the forty-four `0x802DCBFC` destructor adapters from the old
//! `platform::call3` transcription to the shared `game::bases::interface_call`
//! model, which supplies the hidden `r12` descriptor (`param_1 + 0x18` or
//! `param_1 + 0x24`); the remaining nineteen stay `partial`.
//! Evidence is the export at `work/ghidra/rel-d_en_bossNP/export/`.
//!
//! * the module entry point and the global state-list primitives
