//! The eight registrars are the strongest evidence in this REL: every one is
//! tied to a `daEnBoss..._c::StateID_...` string that Ghidra recovered from the
//! data section. Together they register 113 state descriptors, each with the
//! same nine-word copy pattern.
//!
//! ## Start here
//!
//! [`fn_80c00160`] shows how the global state list is linked, and
//! [`fn_80c03880`] is the first complete registrar (Iggy's 18 states). Read a
//! registrar together with the private `register_state` helper to see how the
//! repeated blocks map onto one call per state.
//!
//! For the wave-3 action runners, start with [`fn_80c2f0c0`] (six states, one
//! jump arc) and then read [`fn_80c32800`] (twelve states) to see how the same
//! shape scales. The two share the state counter at `+0x360` and the same
//! animation/animation-controller calls.
//!
//! For wave 4, start with [`fn_80c00d50`] and read the sled action family in
//! address order; the shared model-transform ritual is [`fn_80c01120`]. The
//! large phase dispatchers are [`fn_80c10610`] and [`fn_80c23fd0`].
//!
//! For wave 5, start with [`fn_80c00240`] (the Iggy constructor and its
//! controller elements), then read the two aim solvers [`fn_80c23680`] and
//! [`fn_80c239c0`] together with the heading primitives [`fn_80c12790`] and
