//!
//! ## State-registration data model
//!
//! All eight registrars use the same shapes (`// observed:` in every block):
//!
//! | object | offset | meaning |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | state | `+0x00` | vtable pointer |
//! | state | `+0x0C..+0x2C` | nine descriptor words, copied with a 12-byte rotation |
//! | state | `+0x30` | optional state-id/callback result (only some state families) |
//! | descriptor | `+0x00..+0x20` | nine source words |
//! | list node | `+0x00` | next node |
//! | list node | `+0x04` | per-state runner function pointer |
//! | list node | `+0x08` | state object |
//!
//! The copy rotation is fixed: state `+0x0C` reads descriptor `+0x18`, state
//! `+0x10` reads `+0x1C`, state `+0x14` reads `+0x20`, state `+0x18` reads
//! `+0x0C`, state `+0x1C` reads `+0x10`, state `+0x20` reads `+0x14`, state
//! `+0x24` reads `+0x00`, state `+0x28` reads `+0x04`, and state `+0x2C`
//! reads `+0x08`. It is documented once in `copy_state_descriptor`.
//!
//! The list head is the first word of this REL's BSS: `0x80C6C900`.
//!
//! ## Action-runner data model
//!
//! The six large functions added in wave 3 share one actor layout
//! (`// inferred:` from the repeated field accesses; every offset is exact and
//! comes straight from the export):
//!
//! | offset | meaning |
//! |---|---|
//! | `+0x60` | actor class vtable (`+0x3F0`, `+0x3F4`, `+0x3F8` action slots) |
//! | `+0x102` | 16-bit animation/action selector |
//! | `+0x348` | byte flag reset or set at a state transition |
//! | `+0x360` | 32-bit action-state counter; each runner dispatches on it |
//! | `+0x544` | animation-controller object (`+0x24` plays a clip id) |
//! | `+0x600` | model root used for animation-name lookup |
//! | `+0x604` | model object; vtable slot `+0x1C` updates it every frame |
//! | `+0x644` | animation object tested and rebound at each transition |
//! | `+0xAC/+0xB0/+0xB4` | position x/y/z |
//! | `+0xE8/+0xEC` | horizontal speed / vertical velocity |
//! | `+0x114` | per-frame vertical acceleration |
//!
//! Each state performs the same ritual: call the per-frame virtual update,
//! test whether the current clip finished (`0x80169020`), bind a clip by name
//! (`0x8023A0B0` then `0x801651F0`), set the clip's blend parameters, and
//! increment `+0x360`. States 3/4 and 9/10 in the jump family also integrate a
//! vertical arc by hand to derive the horizontal speed written to `+0xE8`.
//!
//! ## Dependencies
//!
//! [`crate::platform`] supplies volatile byte/word access and the `call0..call6`
//! shims. Everything outside this file is kept as a raw address. Names such as
//! `fn_80c046d0` are reconstruction names, not Nintendo symbols; the REL has no
//! symbol table.
//!
