/// Per-frame spawn, trail and collision manager for one actor family.
///
/// The function walks a table of model/animation entries at `0x80C613D8`
/// (count at `0x80C617F8`, three live words per entry at `+0x424/+0x428/+0x42C`),
/// asks a collision helper for spawn points, fills the ten-entry position
/// array at `+0x130`, and then advances the four `0x140`-byte trail records at
/// `+0x10C0..+0x10D4`. Each trail record carries a counter, an animation handle,
/// a scaled velocity vector, and an index used for the decay formula.
///
/// # Original
/// Synthetic base `0x80C00000`; this address is not a runtime address.
/// `FUN_80c22ca0`, address `0x80C22CA0`, size 2,520 bytes,
/// `work/ghidra/rel-d_en_bossNP/export/80c22ca0_FUN_80c22ca0.c`.
/// - Removed: the modelled `_savegpr_14` prologue call (`0x802DCD40`) and the
///   two `_restgpr_14` epilogue calls (`0x802DCD8C`, one per exit); the image
///   reads the manager from the incoming `r3` (`mr r15,r3`) and has no return.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `manager` - the manager/actor object; the incoming `r3`.
/// * `0x80162D50(0x17, 0)`
/// supplies a related actor used by the collision sweep.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Constructs and destroys temporary controller arrays through
/// `0x802DC9A0`/`0x802DCA98`, reads positions through `0x800E7880`, applies
/// damage/interaction callbacks to nearby actors, and writes the four trail
/// records' counters, handles, velocities and positions.
///
/// # Safety
/// The manager object, every table entry, the ten-entry spawn array and the
/// four trail records must be valid in the synthetic image.
///
/// # Confidence
/// medium - the gameplay body is exact: every spawn, trail and collision step is
/// present with its table bases and offsets. The export's leading
/// paired-single/GQR spills are Ghidra's rendering of the PPC register save area
/// and carry no game state (noted inside the body), and the vtable-slot
/// prototypes and the `0x8065C9A0` `double` arguments are inferred conventions
/// rather than missing code, so the row is `translated`.
