/// lookup. Two of them pass the lookup result together with `this + 0x774` to
/// `0x806EEE20`, so `+0x770` and the three floats at `+0x774..+0x77C` form a
/// handle/vector pair. The same read-then-lookup chain appears inline in
/// [`fn_80c191a0`] and [`fn_80c43670`], which is why the shape is certain even
/// though this copy is out of line.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80c0b510` at `0x80C0B510` (8 bytes)
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80C00000`; this is not a runtime address.
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_en_bossNP/export/80c0b510_FUN_80c0b510.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `this` - object holding the handle word at `+0x770`.
///
/// # Returns
/// The descriptor word of the resolved bank node, or `0` when the handle does
/// not resolve.
///
/// # Side effects
/// None in this body. The callee reads the eight-bucket hash table at
/// `0x80377A70`.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this + 0x770` must be readable, and the loaded handle must be one the
/// `main.dol` lookup accepts.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - both instructions decode from the raw text, the tail target is
/// relocation-backed and resolves to `0x80162D00`, and the inline siblings in
/// this file prove the `(handle) -> descriptor` shape.
pub unsafe fn fn_80c0b510(this: usize) -> u32 {
    // observed: lwz r3,0x770(r3) ; b 0x80162D00 - the loaded handle is r3.
    platform::call1(0x8016_2D00, platform::read_u32(this + 0x770))
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Position-effect spawner (0x80C20000 bucket, wave 118)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// The last untranslated entry of the `0x80C20000` bucket sits between the
// clamped-ratio helper `0x80C22580` (`fn_80c22580`) and the wide castle runner
// `0x80C22CA0` (`fn_80c22ca0`). Its Ghidra C export stops at `halt_baddata()`,
// so the body below was decoded from the raw REL text
// (`work/rels/d_en_bossNP.rel`, text section 1, file offset
// `address - 0x80C00000`) and the tail branch was resolved from the module-0
// `R_PPC_REL24` entry in the REL relocation stream (`0x7EA60`).

/// Spawns effect type `0x105` at a caller-supplied position.
///
/// `// observed:` the raw text is ten instructions:
/// `lwz r0,0x76C(r3)` / `mr r5,r4` / `li r3,0x105` / `li r6,0` /
/// `cntlzw r0,r0` / `li r7,0` / `rlwinm r0,r0,27,31,31` / `neg r4,r0` /
/// `addi r4,r4,0x11` / `b 0x80064610`.
/// The `cntlzw`/`rlwinm`/`neg`/`addi` chain is the compiler's
/// `word == 0 ? 0x10 : 0x11`: `cntlzw` yields `32` for zero and `0..31`
/// otherwise, the rotate keeps one bit of that count, and the negated value
/// added to `0x11` gives `0x10` only when `+0x76C` is zero. The branch leaves
/// `r3 = 0x105`, `r4 = 0x10` or `0x11`, `r5 = param_2`, `r6 = 0`, `r7 = 0`.
///
/// The branch field at `0x80C228C4` carries a module-0 `R_PPC_REL24`
/// relocation with addend `0x80064610`, so the tail target is the `main.dol`
/// effect factory `0x80064610`. That export forwards its first four arguments
/// to `0x8006CA80`, which stores `param_3`/`param_4` through `0x8006CA70` and
/// spawns `param_1`; the same five-argument shape is already used by
/// [`fn_80c32660`], [`fn_80c30760`] and [`fn_80c30820`]. The `main.dol`
/// export is typed `void`, but the chain ends in `0x80162B00`, which returns
/// its `0x80162A70` result in `r3`; both call sites consume that word as a
/// handle, so this body returns it.
///
/// # Original
/// - Ghidra: `FUN_80c228a0` at `0x80C228A0` (40 bytes)
/// - Synthetic base: `0x80C00000`; this is not a runtime address.
/// - Evidence: `work/ghidra/rel-d_en_bossNP/export/80c228a0_FUN_80c228a0.c`
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `this` - castle boss whose `+0x76C` phase word selects the variant.
/// * `position` - position record passed through as the spawner's third
///   argument; the two aim scripts hand it the vector sampled by `0x800E7880`.
///
/// # Returns
/// The spawn handle left in `r3` by `0x80064610` (through `0x80162B00`), or
/// whatever the factory returns when the effect cannot be created.
///
/// # Side effects
/// Spawns effect `0x105` through `0x80064610`, which also writes the global
/// record used by `0x8006CA70`. Nothing in this body writes actor memory.
///
/// # Safety
/// `this + 0x76C` must be readable and `position` must be a record accepted by
/// `0x8006CA80`; the `main.dol` effect factory must be present.
///
/// # Confidence
/// high - all ten instructions decode from the raw text, the tail target is
/// relocation-backed and resolves to `0x80064610`, and both callers in this
/// REL prove the `(actor, position) -> handle` signature. Only the meaning of
/// the `+0x76C` phase word and the `0x10`/`0x11` variants is inferred from
/// neighbouring code.
pub unsafe fn fn_80c228a0(this: usize, position: usize) -> u32 {
    // observed: lwz r0,0x76C(r3) ; cntlzw / rlwinm / neg / addi r4,r4,0x11
    let phase = platform::read_u32(this + 0x76C);
    let variant = if phase == 0 { 0x10 } else { 0x11 };
    // observed: li r3,0x105 ; mr r5,r4 ; li r6,0 ; li r7,0 ; b 0x80064610
    platform::call5(0x8006_4610, 0x105, variant, position as u32, 0, 0)
}

